# How many pages each program of this corpus draws. One basename and
# one count per line.
#
# It is held from both ends: a program of this corpus with no count
# here fails the corpus, so one cannot be added without a count, and a
# count naming a program the corpus does not hold fails it too.
#
# The counts are not a record of what this tree draws -- a count taken
# from that makes whatever the tree does today correct by definition.
# Every program here is one encapsulated illustration and eleven of the
# twelve say so themselves in a %%Pages: 1 line their producer wrote;
# mathematica carries no such line and is the single drawing its one
# showpage ends. An encapsulated file is a figure for another document
# to place, so one page is the shape of the whole corpus and a program
# of it drawing two would be a program that had stopped being one.
